  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal contract obligations in Washington total $12.6B across 76,725 awards with an average award size of $164K. Obligations are down 20.3% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show prior peaks: FY25 was $15.8B and FY24 was $15.4B, while FY22 was $12.1B and FY21 was $15.6B. FY23 recorded $13B. Current-year totals are partial because the period reported is fiscal year to date, so the $12.6B is not a full-year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What agencies account for the largest share of FY2026 spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $8.5B in obligations. The Department of Energy follows with $2.9B. Other agencies with notable obligations include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $271M and the Department of Agriculture at $248M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries lead federal contracting in Washington?",
        "body": "THE BOEING COMPANY is the top vendor with $5.9B in obligations, followed by BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE at $1.1B and HANFORD TANK WASTE OPERATIONS & CLOSURE, LLC at $691M. The largest industry by obligations is Aircraft Manufacturing at $5.9B, then Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $1.1B, and Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal at $698M."
      }
    ]
  },
